</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Additional Ablations</h3>

<section id="A6.SS2.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Effect of no Robustness (<math id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>)</h4>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ Effect of no Robustness (𝜌=0) ‣ F.2 Additional Ablations ‣ Appendix F Additional Results and Ablations ‣ Preference Robustness for DPO with Applications to Public Health" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> presents results for a variant of <span id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DPO-PRO</span> with <math id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>, which effectively removes the DRO component. In this case, the method reduces to a form of DPO that uses soft preference probabilities <math id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> instead of binary labels. Interestingly, the performance remains slightly better than vanilla DPO. We note that when <math id="A6.SS2.SSSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss becomes a standard cross-entropy between probability scores.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Flip Noise - Win Rate (%) and Evaluation Reward Comparison. DPO-PRO with <math id="A6.T8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<table id="A6.T8.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T8.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
